{
  "_comment": [
    "Visit profiles, the assessment catalog, and the rules that decide who may",
    "staff a visit. All of it data: no coordinator name, assessment name or",
    "rule appears in a Python conditional anywhere.",
    "",
    "WHY A CATALOG AND NOT A LIST OF NAMES. Two assessments that read alike are",
    "not interchangeable. CSBS Modified at 6m and standard CSBS at 9-12m are",
    "separate rows with separate codes, so being signed off on one never grants",
    "the other. That is the single most dangerous thing a scheduler could get",
    "wrong here, and it is prevented by the shape of the data rather than by",
    "anyone remembering.",
    "",
    "ALTERNATIVE GROUPS. A sibling evaluation needs ADOS plus Mullen OR DAS.",
    "Requirements carrying the same alternative_group are satisfied by any one",
    "of them; everything else must be held individually.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS TRANSCRIBED AND WHAT IS A PLACEHOLDER. The assessment codes, the",
    "visit schedules, the durations and the settings come from the ESD Lab",
    "Scheduling Manual. The pairing constraints and special rules are the",
    "shapes those rules take, seeded with the examples discussed, and every one",
    "of them ships inactive with an owner field to fill in. An inactive rule",
    "changes nothing until somebody who knows the case turns it on."
  ],
  "confirmed": false,

